                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Did you like POVRAY graphics in the 90s? Then this game is for you!\n\nThe 'adventure puzzles' are ridiculous (90% of them involving a magic scroll to solve problems). The other puzzles are just dumbed down versions of ones you can find in better games (for example a match-the-shape one that's more suited for a three year old). It feels like a cheap hidden object game just without the hidden object scenes.\n\nThe graphics are basic 3D rendered scenes that feel absolutely lifeless. You can see on the screenshots that it's barely better than early 90s 3D rendered pictures. This wouldn't be a problem if the game was actually good and engaging, but it surely isn't.\n\nThe voice acting is decent and the cut scenes have at least some effort put into them. The story itself though is very generic and quite boring.\n\nThere's nothing in this 'game' that makes it worth playing. There are better free games out there. Much better games...\n",
